{
  "_note": "Per-dataset SPEC-CARD fields. These cards describe THE ATLAS, not the slice we happen to work on: `cells`, `schema` tier counts and `timepoints` are all full-published-object numbers, with `workingSlice` naming our subset where one exists. Joined on `id` to dataset_facts.json (still the source of truth for METHOD/platform and the cluster counts in the summary strip); dataset_facts.json is never modified. Values are read live from the backing .h5ad / author metadata, transcribed from repo prose, or supplied by Steven — see `_provenance`. Anything unsourced is the literal string \"TBD\". Where a field is not a gap but a genuine absence, it says so in words (\"Unannotated — labelling target\", \"N/A\") rather than TBD.",
  "_provenance": {
    "cells_and_slices": "Full-object n_obs read in backed mode. zscape 3,231,733 (obs[timepoint]==48 -> 813,782, matches facts.cells). daniocell 336,603 (36-72 hpf window -> 191,832, matches facts.cells). chemfish 2,068,668 (timepoint==48 -> 1,579,675, which is what facts.fullCells records; facts.cells 250,000 is our uniform sample of that). commit_gold 209,639 is the benchmark definition itself, not a subsample, so no working-slice line. megafin/megafin_parse/minifin are used whole.",
    "timepoints": "Read from obs, never inferred. zscape obs[timepoint] = 18 values (18-48 in 2h steps, +72, +96). commit_gold obs[timepoint] = single value 48. daniocell obs[hpf] = 39 values (18-96). chemfish cell_metadata timepoint = 36/48/72. megafin/megafin_parse/minifin have NO timepoint column — single-collection designs, so they keep EXPOSURE -> COLLECTION rows.",
    "schema": "Native label hierarchies, exact column names, counted on the full objects. zscape obs[tissue]/obs[cell_type_broad]/obs[cell_type_sub]. chemfish cell_metadata tissue/cell_type. daniocell obs[tissue.name]/obs[tissue.figure]/obs[clust]. Counts are NOT comparable across datasets — the tiers are different granularities, which is why the cards show the hierarchy rather than a normalised number.",
    "genes": "n_vars. zscape + commit_gold + chemfish 32,031; daniocell 30,121; megafin_parse + minifin 32,520; megafin (Lawson) 36,351.",
    "zscape_perturbations": "obs[gene_target] = 34: 28 knockouts + 6 ctrl-* arms. Matches the published spec card exactly.",
    "chemfish_perturbations": "cell_metadata obs[perturbation] = 11 (8 compounds + DMSO/EtOH/novehicle), obs[target] = 8 (7 pathways + Control). Confirms the published spec card exactly.",
    "megafin_perturbations": "Decoded from obs[sample] (Manual) / obs[samples] (Parse) — identical 93-well sets, format m1_<well>_CP01_<compound>_<dose>. 46 compounds = 45 small molecules + Sorafenib positive control, matching designFacts. The 3 QC-removed wells (Vorinostat 1uM/B11, Romidepsin 5uM/C3, Dinaciclib 5uM/E3) dropped ONE DOSE each, not the compound — all 46 survive in the object, so all 46 are listed and the dropped wells are noted in the summary line.",
    "minifin_perturbations": "obs[perturbation] = 4 (DMSO, Dapagliflozin, Orlistat, Sorafenib) across obs[sample] = 43 replicate samples (DMSO 11, Dapagliflozin 10, Orlistat 11, Sorafenib 11). Spelling taken from obs[perturbation]; obs[sample] misspells it 'Dapaglifozan'.",
    "footers": "MegaFIN + MiniFin pathway/target footers deferred to Steven — they need a target annotation he supplies.",
    "zebrahub": "Read from /data/datasets/raw_datasets/Zebrahub/. zebrahub_combined.h5ad = 101,833 x 32,060, verified equal to the sum of the 10 per-stage v1 releases (1,251 + 6,699 + 3,862 + 3,862 + 6,297 + 5,899 + 12,914 + 15,483 + 24,987 + 20,579). Timepoints from obs[timepoint] (10 values, native mixed hpf/dpf labels kept as published). Schema = obs[zebrafish_anatomy_ontology_class] = 147, a single ZFA-backed tier (obs[zebrafish_anatomy_ontology_id] is the same 147 as ZFA IDs). The dataset README maps 2dpf -> 48 hpf, which is why the 2dpf pill carries the 48-hpf highlight. NOT in the wizard chooser and has no DatasetDef — reference card only.",
    "summary": "One-line high-level description per card, max 50 words, condensed from prose already in the repo (DatasetDef blurbs in KasperovClient.tsx, dataset_facts source/design/subsample) plus the counts verified in this file. Descriptive only - introduces no number that isn't already sourced elsewhere in this file.",
    "name": "Card names track the datasets themselves; 'ZSCAPE Classic' is shown as 'ZSCAPE' here. The wizard chooser's own DatasetDef name is unchanged (KasperovClient.tsx is not touched), so the chooser row still reads 'ZSCAPE Classic'.",
    "megafin_doses": "Doses decoded from the well names: every compound is 1 uM and 5 uM except the three whose one dose was QC-removed — Vorinostat (SAHA) survives at 5 uM only, Romidepsin (FK228) and Dinaciclib (SCH727965) at 1 uM only. 46 compounds -> 89 dose-pills. Matches facts.design's QC list exactly.",
    "minifin_doses": "MiniFin has NO dose data: no dose column in obs, no dose in obs[sample], nothing in the Parse report metadata (all-sample/report/*, process/run_proc_def.json). The 43 samples are REPLICATES (numbered 1-6 plus a 'b' batch) — DMSO 11, Dapagliflozin 10, Orlistat 11, Sorafenib 11 — not two doses. Concentration left unstated rather than guessed.",
    "zfa_schema": "ZFA target schema + vocabulary counts supplied by Steven. Applied to the three unannotated internal atlases (MegaFin x2, MiniFin) as the schema we label INTO — they carry no annotation of their own today, which the row's note keeps explicit. The ~3,107-term figure agrees with the frozen ZFA option menu already cited in the Commit Gold blurb.",
    "megafin_manual_date": "2026-06-14 — the Manual/Lawson rebuild's completion. Corroborated two ways: mtime of /data/scratch/bench/megafin_rebuild_src.h5ad (2026-06-14 02:52) and repo commit 07a3ef19 'DanioType combined pass: finalize MegaFin rebuild' (2026-06-14). Not a recorded build-date field — none exists.",
    "genome_annotation": "Genome build + GTF per dataset. ZSCAPE / ChemFish / DanioCell: GRCz11 with Lawson Lab Zebrafish Transcriptome Annotation v4.3.2 (harmonises Ensembl+RefSeq, improved 3'UTRs, extra gene models) — published methods; ZSCAPE and ChemFish corroborate locally by sharing an identical 32,031-gene universe. MiniFin + MegaFin Parse: GRCz11 read straight out of process/run_proc_def.json (Parse split-pipe v1.7.1, genome_names 'GRcZ11', 32,520 genes); the Ensembl release is not recorded there, so it stays TBD. MegaFin ZSB: Lawson LL IDs in var[ll_id] (36,351 genes) — Lawson annotation is defined on GRCz11; the exact version is not recorded on-instance. Zebrahub: GRCz11 — but the citation found is Zebrahub-MULTIOME (Cell Ranger ARC 2.0.2 on Ensembl GRCz11), a sibling assay, not the scRNA atlas on this card. Verify before relying on it.",
    "zebrahub_capture": "Whole-cell, from Lange et al. 2024 (Cell) methods: an optimised cell-dissociation protocol avoiding embryo pooling, suspensions counted at 700-1200 cells/ul and loaded on the Chromium Controller. The nuclei-based protocol belongs to Zebrahub-Multiome, a different assay.",
    "zscape_groups": "Grouping derived from the naming convention in obs[gene_target], NOT from a genotype column — none exists. '-mut' suffix = stable mutant line; a hyphen joining two gene symbols = double knockout; bare symbol = single-gene F0 crispant. Corroborated by the data: hgfa/hgfa-mut, mafba/mafba-mut, met/met-mut, noto/noto-mut, tbx16/tbx16-mut all appear as SEPARATE targets (which only makes sense as crispant vs mutant of the same gene), and four of the five mutant genes have a matching sibling control arm (ctrl-hgfa, ctrl-mafba, ctrl-met, ctrl-noto). 18 single + 5 double + 5 mutant = 28.",
    "chemfish_doses": "Per-compound concentrations from cell_metadata dose/dose_type: Cyclopamine 100, DEAB 10, DMH1 40, LY411575 10, SB505124 50, SU5402 20, WntC59 20, A8301 50 (all micromolar). Each compound has exactly ONE concentration — unlike MegaFin, ChemFish is not a two-dose design. Dosing timepoints from obs[drug_addition] = 6/13/24/36/42 hpf; collection from obs[timepoint] = 36/48/72 hpf. Only the 6 and 13 hpf dosing arms were collected at all three timepoints; 24/36/42 hpf dosing was collected at 48 hpf only."
  },
